/* VPinOS theme -- colors sampled directly from the actual logo
 * (config/bootloaders/splash.svg's embedded PNG): black background,
 * vivid cyan-blue accent (#01B4FE, from the "OS" text/neon glow), red
 * accent (#FD1B1E, from the flipper bumpers).
 *
 * Deliberately scoped to the sidebar + buttons only, NOT the main
 * content area -- confirmed directly (real screenshots) that forcing
 * #mainApp to black/white broke several individual install modules
 * (partition chooser, location map): their labels paint text via
 * QPalette/custom widgets rather than respecting a QSS `color`
 * override, so the text stayed black -- invisible on a black
 * background. The sidebar (SidebarBackground/SidebarText/etc. in
 * branding.desc, which is what #sidebarApp/#logoApp correspond to
 * under the hood -- see that file's own comment) renders correctly
 * because those are Calamares's own dedicated, tested styling hooks;
 * the main content area isn't, so it stays at its normal light
 * default rather than fighting every module's own internal styling.
 *
 * Object-name IDs (#mainApp, #sidebarApp, #logoApp) are Calamares's
 * own C++ object names, not something we chose -- see the branding
 * component's own documented example (calamares's default branding
 * stylesheet.qss) for how these were found (Debug Dialog -> Tools ->
 * Widget Tree).
 */

QPushButton {
    background-color: #01B4FE;
    color: #000000;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 6px 14px;
}

QPushButton:hover {
    background-color: #3BC4FF;
}

QPushButton:pressed {
    background-color: #0090CC;
}

QPushButton:disabled {
    background-color: #2A2A2A;
    color: #808080;
}
